    "wacc_rationale": "Cost of equity 10.5% built in AUD: Australian 10-year government bond ~4.4% (Sep-2026) + beta ~1.1 x 5.5% equity risk premium = ~10.5%. Single rate across scenarios; risk lives in the scenario flows and weights.",
    "notes": "MODEL: distributable Underlying NPAT at cost of equity, built segment-by-segment and summed. AMP is a diversified financial group straddling two routing rows: a bank (AMP Bank, $23.7bn loans, $17.8bn deposits, $10.1bn wholesale/RMBS funding) and capital-light fee businesses (Platforms/North, Superannuation & Investments, NZ Wealth; $167.6bn AUM) plus equity-accounted China partnerships (CLPC 19.99%, CLAMP 14.97%) and PCCP. Per dcf-methods SKILL.md the parts are valued separately and summed: each segment's TTM underlying NPAT is projected on its own growth path, summed to group underlying NPAT, reduced by a below-the-line leakage (business simplification, litigation, remediation - present in every year since 2019) to a statutory proxy, then by capital retained for growth (mainly AMP Bank loan growth and RSE/AFSL capital creep) to distributable earnings, which are discounted at a single AUD cost of equity and capitalised at min(Gordon, exit P/E cap). An owner-FCF DCF is NOT usable: FY25 OCF was -1,375m on -806m loan and -939m deposit movements; reported FCF is meaningless. NET DEBT: interest-bearing liabilities of $28.8bn are AMP Bank deposits and wholesale funding plus $330m bank sub-debt (regulatory capital) and $480m corporate MTNs whose interest ($16m/half) is already inside Partnerships & Group NPAT - none is deducted (flows are post-interest). The bridge instead adds the two items that are genuinely distributable over and above earnings: the Group CET1 surplus of $322m at 30-Jun-2026 (management is returning it via a second $150m buyback tranche in 2H26) and the $418m net deferred tax asset, which CET1 excludes and which converts to capital as utilised (+$56m in 1H26; cash tax paid was $18m in FY25 against ~$120m of underlying tax expense) - taken at $300m PV. Under the excluded-income rule the after-tax interest the surplus earns (~$9m/yr) is stripped from the Y1 Group segment. Equity-accounted stakes ($890m carrying) stay OUT of the bridge because their earnings ($56m from China in 1H26) stay IN the flows. SHARE COUNT: held flat at the fully diluted 30-Jun-2026 count (2,432.8m issued - 2.1m treasury + ~45m dilutive rights per the FY25 diluted/basic gap) because SBC ($22m TTM) is expensed inside controllable costs and therefore inside underlying NPAT. The 2H26 $150m buyback tranche is not pre-modelled: the cash sits in the CET1 surplus and the shares in the count, which is internally consistent at 30 June; buying back at or above intrinsic value is at best value-neutral per share. COST OF EQUITY 10.5% in AUD: ~4.4% AGB 10yr + ~1.1 beta x 5.5% ERP, held identical across scenarios so risk is charged once, in the flows. PRICE: A$2.55 regular ASX close 21-Sep-2026, which is the 52-week high (range 1.14-2.55). ENGINE MAPPING: the component fields exist so the dashboard rebuilds the same number - revenue is a total-revenue proxy, ebitda margin = (underlying pre-tax + SBC)/revenue, 30% tax returns underlying NPAT, and capex_pct carries leakage + retention. Sliders labelled EBITDA margin/capex are therefore 'underlying pre-tax margin' and 'leakage + retention' for this ticker."
